Fix positive integers $K^2$ and $\chi$, and consider the moduli space $\mathcal{M}_{K^2,\chi}$ of canonical models of complex projective surfaces of general type with self-intersection of the canonical class equal to $K^2$ and holomorphic Euler characteristic equal to $\chi$. Let $M$ be an irreducible component of $\mathcal{M}_{K^2,\chi}$.

Determine geometric or numerical conditions on $M$ (equivalently, on the general surface parametrized by $M$ and its invariants) that guarantee the existence of a flat projective family $\pi : \mathcal{X} \to \Delta$ over the complex disc $\Delta$ such that:
\begin{itemize}
\item the general fibre $\pi^{-1}(t)$, for $t \in \Delta \setminus \{0\}$, is isomorphic to the general surface parametrized by $M$;
\item the central fibre $\pi^{-1}(0)$ is an irreducible, reduced rational surface.
\end{itemize}

In other words, characterize when the general surface of general type in a component $M$ admits a one-parameter flat degeneration to an irreducible, reduced rational surface.

